\title{ensembleweather: the official R client for the Ourea probabilistic weather API}
\description{
Ourea serves ensemble weather forecasts: every value is a distribution
computed by the server from the full set of model members. This package
asks for those distributions and returns them as tibbles.
}
\details{
Start with \code{\link[=ew_forecast]{ew_forecast()}}. Ask for the chance of crossing a threshold with
\code{\link[=ew_chance]{ew_chance()}}, and for a storm total's distribution with \code{\link[=ew_total]{ew_total()}}.
Errors are classed conditions (see \link{ensembleweather_error}). Calls work
without an API key (the Free tier); see \code{\link[=ew_client]{ew_client()}} for keys, units,
retries and the cache.

The package never sums, averages or interpolates quantiles and never
derives a probability from them: the server computes every probability and
window total from the full ensemble, and the package only carries them.
}
